# Claude Code
#
# The project's own instructions and the skill workflow are tracked: README
# advertises them as part of what this repo is, every skill tells its reader to
# consult CLAUDE.md, and a file git does not see is a file nothing reviews —
# which is how CLAUDE.md's "Movie Import" section stayed wrong for the whole
# `movie-form` initiative. Decided in issue 110.
#
# What stays out is machine-local state: the permission allow-list is full of
# this machine's absolute paths, and the lock file is a running process's. The
# git guardrail is a deny rule in that machine-local file rather than the hook
# under `hooks/`, which is why that script carries a note saying it is inert.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

